.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_GET_SERIALNUMBER 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_get_serialNumber ,
.Nm X509_get0_serialNumber ,
.Nm X509_set_serialNumber ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_get0_serialNumber ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_set1_serialNumber
.Nd get or set certificate serial number
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft ASN1_INTEGER *
.Fo X509_get_serialNumber
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_INTEGER *
.Fo X509_get0_serialNumber
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_set_serialNumber
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "ASN1_INTEGER *serial"
.Fc
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft ASN1_INTEGER *
.Fo X509_ACERT_get0_serialNumber
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_set1_serialNumber
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "ASN1_INTEGER *serial"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_get_serialNumber
returns the serial number of certificate
.Fa x
as an
.Vt ASN1_INTEGER
structure which can be examined or initialised.
The value returned is an internal pointer which
.Sy MUST NOT
be freed up after the call.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_serialNumber
is the same as
.Fn X509_get_serialNumber
except it accepts a const parameter and returns a const result.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set_serialNumber
sets the serial number of certificate
.Fa x
to
.Fa serial .
A copy of the serial number is used internally so
.Fa serial
should be freed up after use.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_serialNumber
performs the same operation as
.Fn X509_get_serialNumber
for attribute certificates.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_set1_serialNumber
performs the same operation as
.Fn X509_set_serialNumber
for attribute certificates.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_get_serialNumber ,
.Fn X509_get0_serialNumber
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_serialNumber
return a pointer to an
.Vt ASN1_INTEGER
structure.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set_serialNumber
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_set1_serialNumber
return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr d2i_X509 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr X509_CRL_get0_by_serial 3 ,
.Xr X509_get0_signature 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_ext_d2i 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_extension_flags 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_pubkey 3 ,
.Xr X509_get_subject_name 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_add_entry_by_txt 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_object 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_get_index_by_NID 3 ,
.Xr X509_NAME_print_ex 3 ,
.Xr X509_new 3 ,
.Xr X509_sign 3 ,
.Xr X509V3_get_d2i 3 ,
.Xr X509_verify_cert 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn X509_get_serialNumber
and
.Fn X509_set_serialNumber
functions are available in all versions of OpenSSL. The
.Fn X509_get0_serialNumber
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.0. The
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_serialNumber
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_set1_serialNumber
functions were added in OpenSSL 3.4.
